        {
          "contents": "",
          "post_id": "469349",
          "text": "<p>$m$ identical balls are to be placed in $n$ distinct bags. You are given that $m \\geq kn$, where $k$ is a natural number $\\geq 1$. In how many ways can the balls be placed in the bags if each bag must contain at least $k$ balls?</p><ol start=\"1\" style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\"><li>$\\left( \\begin{array}{c} m - k \\\\ n - 1 \\end{array} \\right)$<br> </li><li>$\\left( \\begin{array}{c} m - kn + n - 1 \\\\ n - 1 \\end{array} \\right)$<br> </li><li>$\\left( \\begin{array}{c} m - 1 \\\\ n - k \\end{array} \\right)$<br> </li><li>$\\left( \\begin{array}{c} m - kn + n + k - 2 \\\\ n - k \\end{array} \\right)$</li></ol>",
          "type": "Multiple Choice",
          "answer": "b",
          "award": 2,
          "penalty": "0.6666",
          "tags": "goclasses_cs_wq14,goclasses,discrete-mathematics,combinatory,two-marks",
